VALUES ('f3f5dbc5-cf02-451a-86e1-d468921720f0', '1998', 'COMSATS University Islamabad (CUI) is a public sector university chartered by the Federal Government of Pakistan in 2018 (originally established as CIIT in 1998). CUI functions under the governance of the Ministry of Science and Technology. The university comprises 7 physical campuses - Islamabad (Main Campus), Lahore, Abbottabad, Wah Cantt, Attock, Sahiwal, and Vehari - plus a Virtual Campus that is currently not operational and is seeking HEC NOC to launch distance learning programs. It hosts 6 faculties, 23 academic departments, 6 research centers, and over 39,000 enrolled students. CUI has consistently ranked among top national universities and leading international institutions according to Times Higher Education (THE) and QS World University Rankings.', 'The COMSATS University Islamabad, founded in the belief that understanding enriches all people, is dedicated to the search for truth through advancement of learning and extending the frontiers of knowledge; to the sharing of this knowledge through education in an academically diverse range of disciplines and subjects; and to the application of this knowledge to benefit the people of Pakistan, the Muslim Ummah, and the World, at large.', 'https://www.comsats.edu.pk/assets/img/COMSATS-logo.png', 'https://www.comsats.edu.pk/assets/img/all-campuses.jpg', '39100', 'https://www.comsats.edu.pk', 'admissions@comsats.edu.pk', '+92-51-90495032')
